{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-106832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2x-{x}^{3}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-106832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rewrite the limit as\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2x-{x}^{3}}={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{3}-2x}.\n$$\n\nThe numerator here is a bounded, oscillating function with\n\n$$\n|\\operatorname{sin}⁡x|\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHowever, the denominator ${x}^{3}-2x$ grows without bound as $x\\to \\infty .$ So the denominator is growing much faster than the numerator, and we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2x-{x}^{3}}={lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{x}^{3}-2x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe can see this from the graph of $y=\\frac{-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{2x-{x}^{3}},$ shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/assets/a9d96a5a85181cddc6eb1bd5f79d6a0238ef16f060ddebf2dc4c48ef1911604f.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-106832" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4785cca81f00ae4ef6ae1ebdd939632cbb2b235b76c9125be2de0976f4860a0a"} {"question" "q-106832" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-106832" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "\\infty "] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-106832" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-351278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{9{x}^{2}-6x+20}{(2{x}^{2}+5)x}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{9{x}^{2}-6x+20}{(2{x}^{2}+5)x}=\\,$ | $x\\,-\\,${{field-1}} | $+$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2{x}^{2}+5$ |  | $x$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-351278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9{x}^{2}-6x+20}{(2{x}^{2}+5)x}=\\frac{x+B}{2{x}^{2}+5}+\\frac{4}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(2{x}^{2}+5)x$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}-6x+20 & =(x+B)x+4(2{x}^{2}+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(1)^{2}-6(1)+20 & =(1+B)(1)+4(2(1)^{2}+5) \\\\ 23 & =1+B+28 \\\\ B & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{9{x}^{2}-6x+20}{(2{x}^{2}+5)x}=\\frac{x-6}{2{x}^{2}+5}+\\frac{4}{x}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-351278" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4785cca81f00ae4ef6ae1ebdd939632cbb2b235b76c9125be2de0976f4860a0a"} {"question" "q-351278" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-351278" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-74654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{6+\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-74654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here, the denominator is the imaginary number $4\\text{i}.$ Note that this can be written as $0+4\\text{i},$ so the conjugate is $0-4\\text{i},$ or simply $-4\\text{i}.$\n\nSo, we multiply both the numerator and the denominator by $-4\\text{i},$ so that the denominator turns into a real number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{6+\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}} & =\\frac{6+\\text{i}}{4\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{-4\\text{i}}{-4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-24\\text{i}-4{\\text{i}}^{2}}{-16{\\text{i}}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-24\\text{i}-4(-1)}{-16(-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-24\\text{i}}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that the denominator is a real number, we can write the complex number in the form $a+b\\text{i}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4-24\\text{i}}{16} & =\\frac{4}{16}-\\frac{24}{16}\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-74654" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4785cca81f00ae4ef6ae1ebdd939632cbb2b235b76c9125be2de0976f4860a0a"} {"question" "q-74654" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-74654" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{4}-\\frac{1}{2}\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-74654" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{3}{2}\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-17124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the distance from a point $P$ to the origin is $\\frac{1}{3},$ and that $P$ makes an angle of $\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ with the positive $x$-axis, what are the Cartesian coordinates of $P?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-17124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We notice that the point $P$ is described using polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ where\n\n$$\nr=\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{4}.\n$$\n\nTo convert from polar coordinates to Cartesian coordinates, we use\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate the $x$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ x & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen we calculate the $y$-coordinate of $P:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{4}) \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{-\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ y & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Cartesian coordinates of $P$ are $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-17124" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4785cca81f00ae4ef6ae1ebdd939632cbb2b235b76c9125be2de0976f4860a0a"} {"question" "q-17124" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-17124" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})"] ["math" "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3})"] ["math" "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4})"] ["math" "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{5})"] ["math" "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-17124" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-127838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The vector $u$ has magnitude $6$, the vector $v$ has magnitude $4$, the angle between $u$ and $v$ is ${30}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $u\\times v.$ Find $u\\times v$ in terms of $n.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-127838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =|u|\\cdot |v|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =6\\cdot 4\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =24\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot n \\\\  & =12n.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-127838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4785cca81f00ae4ef6ae1ebdd939632cbb2b235b76c9125be2de0976f4860a0a"} {"question" "q-127838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-127838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "12n"] ["math" "18n"] ["math" "24n"] ["math" "4n"] ["math" "6n"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-127838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12n"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-65463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Simplify $\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-1}-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-65463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply the numerator and the denominator of the fraction by $\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1.$ This gives: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-1} & =\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x-1}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1}{\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1)}{{csc}^{2}⁡x-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the identity ${csc}^{2}⁡\\theta -1={cot}^{2}⁡\\theta $, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1)}{{csc}^{2}⁡x-1}-1 & =\\frac{{cot}^{2}⁡x\\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1)}{{cot}^{2}⁡x}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{cot}^{2}⁡x}\\,(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1)}{\\cancel{{cot}^{2}⁡x}}-1 \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{csc}⁡x+1)\\,-1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-65463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4785cca81f00ae4ef6ae1ebdd939632cbb2b235b76c9125be2de0976f4860a0a"} {"question" "q-65463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-65463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x"] ["math" "1-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x"] ["math" "{csc}^{2}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-65463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{csc}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-328382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The center of the hyperbola ${x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}-6x-36y=54$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-328382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}-6x-36y & =54 \\\\ {x}^{2}-6x-9{y}^{2}-36y & =54 \\\\ [{x}^{2}-6x]-9[{y}^{2}+4y] & =54 \\\\ [(x-3)^{2}-9]-9[(y+2)^{2}-4] & =54 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9-9(y+2)^{2}+36 & =54 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9(y+2)^{2} & =54+9-36 \\\\ (x-3)^{2}-9(y+2)^{2} & =27 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{27})^{2}}-\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{27})^{2}}-\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,3,-2\\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-328382" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4785cca81f00ae4ef6ae1ebdd939632cbb2b235b76c9125be2de0976f4860a0a"} {"question" "q-328382" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-328382" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-328382" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-328382" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-288444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The following equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}+3x+b=-2{x}^{2}+3x-6\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of the constant $b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-288444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nWe compare the constant terms on both sides. On the left-hand side, the constant is $b.$ On the right-hand side, the constant is $-6.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nb=-6.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-288444" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4785cca81f00ae4ef6ae1ebdd939632cbb2b235b76c9125be2de0976f4860a0a"} {"question" "q-288444" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-288444" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-3"] ["math" "-6"] ["math" "0"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-288444" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-134016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/assets/e2d51071ddc198adecdff56593dec29ba9aef10d90b89ddc03a4cdbe9c757034.png)\n\nWhat is the slope of the trend line shown above?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-134016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that the trend line passes through the points $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(0,8)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(3,7).$\n\nTherefore, we compute the slope $m$ of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7-8}{3-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{-1}{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-134016" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4785cca81f00ae4ef6ae1ebdd939632cbb2b235b76c9125be2de0976f4860a0a"} {"question" "q-134016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-134016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{7}"] ["math" "-\\frac{3}{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"} {"question" "q-134016" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029498/state.json" "file_sha256" "0c7c405d13516b54aba6eb121c0b0e7a48f62dc4c73eb9c9a5a850291389309a"}] "usage" {} "basis" 1204 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
